        "story_eyebrow": "Inside the workshop",
        "story_title": "A real workshop, inside.",
        "story_body_1": "Inside HMP Lowdham Grange — a Category-B men's prison in Nottinghamshire — we've built a 2,000 sq ft workshop where learners take a six-week, OCN-accredited course: from workshop safety and material science through frame construction, mechanics and finishing.",
        "story_body_2": "They earn an OCN Level 2 accreditation in sustainable design and manufacturing. Trusted learners are trained as instructors and help deliver the course. In the final week, frames are taken apart so the materials serve the next cohort — which is also what keeps it affordable.",
        "b2b_fallback": "bbc-rd-b2b.jpg",
        "b2b_image_alt": "The Build to Bond workshop inside HMP Lowdham Grange",
        "b2b_eyebrow": "The follow-on",
        "b2b_title": "A bike that goes home.",
        "b2b_body_1": "The most engaged participants progress to Build to Bond — building a children's bamboo balance bike to gift to their own son, daughter, niece or nephew. That bike they keep. The bike goes home; the father stays inside.",
        "b2b_body_2": "It's built on the evidence that maintaining family contact is one of the strongest predictors of reduced reoffending — people who keep close family ties while in prison are 39% less likely to reoffend (Lord Farmer Review, 2017).",
        "b2b_quote": "Watching the pride on a father's face when he presents a bike to his child is something special.",
